# Elements hero celebrations, revision 2

This is a metadata-only successor to the Plant-only exploratory prototype, not a rewrite of its evidence. The user's 28 October 2026 17:20 direction calls for a coherent recurring thread of substantial celebrations across Elements, rather than one or two isolated surprises. Cooking remains without hero popups. The three Mars rewards are byte-preserved as metadata. Other worlds, including both Atlas versions and historical Elements versions, remain unopted-in.

## Selection and cadence

The actual current `elements-house-and-craft-v1` canonical route has 197 combinations across 30 chapters. Nine events fall at combinations 5, 27, 37, 64, 74, 112, 132, 161 and 182. This is a specific authored selection, not a reusable quota. The closest events are ten combinations apart, and the thread continues into the final sixth of the journey. Exploration can change that spacing; these are canonical witnesses, not a forced pace or unlock schedule.

`selection.json` pins each actual one-based combination and action index, its direct recipe-use count, significance and exact text. Direct recipe counts are witnesses, not a ranking algorithm. Plant, Wheel and Iron are broad material/mechanism hubs. The completed Grain mill, Sailboat, first Printed invitations, Microscope, Soap and Clock mark major new powers even where the graph has only one subsequent recipe.

- Plant opens food, timber, fibres, flowers and later study; the user's poetic hint remains intact.
- Wheel opens turning as a reusable possibility, not a claim that a smooth disc is already a gear or vehicle.
- Grain mill is the complete joined machine, rather than its unattached wheel, gear train or stone. Text celebrates readiness, not an unperformed grinding action.
- Iron is workable metal, rather than raw ore or an unlit hearth.
- Sailboat is the completed craft, not a bare raft. Text says ready; no launch is claimed.
- Printed invitations are actual successful impressions, rather than a block merely carved or inked.
- Microscope opens the possibility of investigating pond life; the actual observation remains a separate action.
- Soap is the finished washing material. Text makes no claim of a bar shape, germ-killing or medical/safety efficacy.
- Clock is the complete housed, readable mechanism, not a pendulum or loose clockwork. Its later ferry-timetable branch grounds the shared-time hint.

No House, ordinary vessels, Juice, meal recap or final River atlas was added merely to fill a quota. Paper is a strong candidate but falls at combination31, crowding Wheel27 and Grain mill37. Glass is foundational but falls close to Plant and shelter; the later complete Microscope gives optics a stronger triumph. Another transport beacon or another food preparation would repeat existing themes. The final story remains the chapter's job, not a second victory popup.

## Trigger and save contract

All nine named Elements outputs are actually complete at creation and have no required fitting slots. Existing accepted-creation milestone grammar therefore needs no runtime change. Mars functional predicates remain unchanged. Existing schema validation still rejects missing or impossible outputs.

Focused headless tests independently pin the selection and route indices, reverse operands at each actual hero event, retain every tangible result, preserve a nine-event queue through JSON and compact saves, guard stale acknowledgements, and test Undo/acknowledgement per real hero. Plant-only and metadata-free saved prefixes at all nine achievement points restore without retroactive new popups; later newly made heroes still fire. An existing pending Plant survives an upgrade without adding historical Wheel or Mill rewards. Every current Elements debug checkpoint remains historical after compact restore.

