Only the `campaignMilestones` map and two old selection expectations change. A new dedicated test and this versioned evidence are additive. The helper implementation is unchanged here; final integration must retain the reactive worker's shared `applyChapterPolicies` composition in `applyMilestones`. No separate UI-only metadata path is introduced. No authored campaign, schema, engine, controller, CSS or icon asset changes.

This author input is an isolated overlay over historical combined565. It is not publishable by itself: final integration also needs reactive chapters, the exact source-successor chain and current count expectations in Atlas integration tests. Old source guards must stay historical and receive exact additive successors, not exemptions or rewritten old pins.

Validation is logical/source/headless only. No browser, native dialog, layout, animation, or human delight testing was performed. The final combined full matrix and publication belong to the integrating worker and root, not this author input.
